26:     the following structure:
27: 
28:     {
29:         "attrs": List[uint64], # e.g. [TAG, HEAD, ENT_IOB, ENT_TYPE]
30:         "tokens": bytes, # Serialized numpy uint64 array with the token data
31:         "spaces": bytes, # Serialized numpy boolean array with spaces data
32:         "lengths": bytes, # Serialized numpy int32 array with the doc lengths
33:         "strings": List[unicode] # List of unique strings in the token data
34:     }
35: 
36:     Strings for the words, tags, labels etc are represented by 64-bit hashes in
37:     the token data, and every string that occurs at least once is passed via the
38:     strings object. This means the storage is more efficient if you pack more
39:     documents together, because you have less duplication in the strings.
